# Content/Chimera/ is REAL hand-authored game content — verb blueprints, footstep
# audio, EVA-suit materials, the sand Niagara systems (SandDrift), ship meshes — and
# belongs in source control. It was wrongly blanket-ignored as "procedurally
# generated", which silently kept ~15 game assets off every fresh clone. If a
# genuinely-generated subdir ever needs excluding, scope the rule to THAT subdir —
# never all of Content/Chimera/.

# Corrupted/malformed directories (non-UTF8 names) — a script mangled an "E:\..."
# Windows path into a literal folder. The old rule escaped the *, matching only a
# literal "E*"; this glob catches the real corrupted dir (E + non-ASCII char).
Chimera/E*/

# Node modules cache (Chimera-local npm; use .pi/npm instead for Pi)
Chimera/node_modules/
Chimera/package.json
Chimera/package-lock.json

# UBT-generated clangd database (regenerate via UBT -Mode=GenerateProjectFiles -VSCode)
Chimera/compile_commands.json

